WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:04.279
(upbeat beatbox music)

00:00:04.279 --> 00:00:05.112
- Ooh.

00:00:08.383 --> 00:00:11.800
- I feel like something's gonna jump out.

00:00:13.344 --> 00:00:15.493
- Opening the box.

00:00:15.493 --> 00:00:18.295
(logo whooshes)
(hinge squeaks)

00:00:18.295 --> 00:00:20.265
- What is your real name?

00:00:20.265 --> 00:00:22.944
- When people ask about the
real name, it's almost like

00:00:22.944 --> 00:00:26.571
we're characters or we're in
a stage play or something.

00:00:26.571 --> 00:00:28.250
- No, but your real name.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.447
I just told you.

00:00:29.447 --> 00:00:32.350
- Does every trans
person transition fully?

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:35.741
- Every trans person's full
transition is different.

00:00:35.741 --> 00:00:37.144
- You don't need to look
like me, you don't need

00:00:37.144 --> 00:00:38.149
to look like you.

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:42.438
- What are some issues that
have come up while dating?

00:00:42.438 --> 00:00:44.964
Oh Lord, sweet baby Jesus.

00:00:44.964 --> 00:00:46.062
We could be here all day.

00:00:46.062 --> 00:00:49.172
- 'cause I don't date the
conventional type of person,

00:00:49.172 --> 00:00:51.030
it makes it a little bit more challenging.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.222
- I've always dated cis men,
but recently I've dated a

00:00:54.222 --> 00:00:58.670
trans guy and the sex
is really, really good.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:01.503
So I'm excited about (laughs).

00:01:01.503 --> 00:01:04.653
- Am I still straight
if I want to fuck you?

00:01:04.653 --> 00:01:06.093
- How rude.

00:01:06.093 --> 00:01:07.063
(laughter)

00:01:07.063 --> 00:01:08.932
- You are attracted to them
because they look female,

00:01:08.932 --> 00:01:12.043
then I don't understand why you
would consider yourself gay.

00:01:12.043 --> 00:01:14.162
- How long do you think that you pass?

00:01:14.162 --> 00:01:15.981
- Ehh (laughs).

00:01:15.981 --> 00:01:18.417
- I see beauty in all
aspects if you are passing

00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:19.508
or not passing.

00:01:19.508 --> 00:01:21.871
- When did you decide to be trans?

00:01:21.871 --> 00:01:24.189
- No, that's not how it works, kids.

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:25.175
None of this is a choice.

00:01:25.175 --> 00:01:26.696
It's a choice whether you're
gonna act on it or not.

00:01:26.696 --> 00:01:28.542
I thought am I gonna be happy for myself

00:01:28.542 --> 00:01:30.102
or miserable for everyone else?

00:01:30.102 --> 00:01:33.464
What happens if/when you change your mind?

00:01:33.464 --> 00:01:34.781
(laughs)

00:01:34.781 --> 00:01:36.310
- Ooh, when are we gonna de-transition?

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:37.539
- I'll have to get my titties removed.

00:01:37.539 --> 00:01:39.736
- How do I ask someone their
preferred pronouns politely

00:01:39.736 --> 00:01:41.603
if I'm unclear?

00:01:41.603 --> 00:01:42.484
That's a good question.

00:01:42.484 --> 00:01:43.611
- Like a human being.

00:01:43.611 --> 00:01:46.351
You ask them a direct, clear question.

00:01:46.351 --> 00:01:48.620
- What if they seem offended?

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:49.918
'cause if I was at
Starbucks and they said,

00:01:49.918 --> 00:01:51.032
"What's your preferred pronoun?"

00:01:51.032 --> 00:01:54.689
I'd be like, bitch, can I get my latte?

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:57.696
- What's the worse thing a cis
person has ever said to you?

00:01:57.696 --> 00:02:00.029
- God doesn't make mistakes.

00:02:01.331 --> 00:02:04.952
They're right, I live
a purpose-driven life.

00:02:04.952 --> 00:02:07.896
- During my military
experience, we're clearly like

00:02:07.896 --> 00:02:11.453
I look masculine, my military
documentation says I'm

00:02:11.453 --> 00:02:14.722
a masculine person, but the
records for the military

00:02:14.722 --> 00:02:17.968
didn't say that I was
masculine, so the military law

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:20.651
says that they can still
call me female even though

00:02:20.651 --> 00:02:22.862
you know you have a medical
team and you have all--

00:02:22.862 --> 00:02:24.260
- And you fought for this country.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:29.143
- If you could tell cis people
one thing, what would it be?

00:02:29.143 --> 00:02:30.464
(exhales loudly)

00:02:30.464 --> 00:02:33.534
- The murder rate of trans
women, especially trans women

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:35.284
of color, is so high.

00:02:36.339 --> 00:02:37.951
- You don't have to understand
us, you don't have to

00:02:37.951 --> 00:02:42.200
understand every single gender
identity or trans experience

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.303
in the world, but you can respect us.

00:02:44.303 --> 00:02:46.171
- You need to stop
projecting onto other people

00:02:46.171 --> 00:02:48.854
what you think is normal
because it's not normal,

00:02:48.854 --> 00:02:50.003
it's common.

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.898
- We just need your support.

00:02:51.898 --> 00:02:53.767
- And your understanding.

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:54.974
- And your love.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.557
- And one million dollars each.

00:02:58.482 --> 00:03:00.862
- I need one million and one
because I don't want to spend a

00:03:00.862 --> 00:03:03.938
dollar and be like oh my God,
I'm not a millionaire anymore.

00:03:03.938 --> 00:03:07.381
(logo whooshes)
(hinge squeaks)

